window.MONSTER_CHUNK_137 = [{"name":"Magmoid","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"outsider","subtypes":["earth","extraplanar","fire"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["fiery aura (10 ft., 1d6 fire, Fort DC 17 resists)"],"ac":22,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, -1 size","hp":75,"hd":"10d10+20","hdvalue":10,"fort":9,"ref":10,"will":5,"dr":"10/piercing","immunities":["fire","elemental traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"slam +11 (2d6+2 plus 2d6 fire)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"0 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"burn"},{"type":"magma blast","details":"40 ft. line, 2d6 fire damage, Ref DC 17 half, useable every 1d4 rounds"},{"type":"melt weapons","details":"Fort DC 17"}],"strength":14,"dexterity":17,"constitution":15,"intelligence":4,"wisdom":11,"charisma":10,"baseatk":10,"cmb":13,"cmd":27,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Improved Overrun"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":14}],"languages":["Ignan","Terran (cannot speak)"],"environments":["any (Elemental Plane of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This elemental appears to be a massive of spherical ball entirely comprised of swirling liquid fire and rock.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Burn","kind":"Ex","details":"The body of a magmoid is composed of molten rock and elemental fire. Any melee hit deals 2d6 points of fire damage initially and 1d6 points of damage for the next 1d3 rounds. Creatures attacking a magmoid unarmed or with natural weapons take fire damage each time one of their attacks hits just as if the magmoid had hit with a melee attack."},{"type":"Magma Blast","kind":"Ex","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds as a standard action, a magmoid can release a line of magma to a range of 40 ft. This deals 2d6 points of damage in the round it hits a foe (DC 17 Reflex save for half), and 1d6 points of damage for another 1d3 rounds (no save)."},{"type":"Melt Weapons","kind":"Ex","details":"Any metal weapon that strikes a magmoid must make a successful DC 17 Fortitude save or melt away into slag. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Magmoids are giant balls of elemental magma that destroy or burn anything and everything they come in contact with. Though they are typically only found on the Planes of Earth or Fire or the Plane of Molten Skies (see the City of Brass by Necromancer Games for details on this demiplane), occasionally one slips through a portal or nexus into the Material Plane (usually in the heart of a volcano) where it wreaks havoc upon all things that cross its path; be it creatures, structures, or anything else not immune to fire. Attempts by arcane spellcasters (foolish arcane spellcasters some would say) to control or harness the power of a magmoid, thus far have failed. Magmoids seem to serve no purpose in the Ecology of their native plane and are thought to be a living extension of the plane itself. Small bubbling pockets on the magmoid's form serve as sensory organs. A giant magmoid, measuring 30 ft. across is thought to exist near the Sea of Fire, though none have ever seen it. A magmoid attacks by spraying a blast of superheated magma at opponents or by slamming into and rolling over them. It often targets weapon-wielding creatures first and moves close enough where they can hit with their weapons. The magmoid knows that more than likely should a weapon hit its fiery form, it will be turned into a pile of slag in short order.","ecology":"of their native plane and are thought to be a living extension of the plane itself. Small bubbling pockets on the magmoid's form serve as sensory organs. A giant magmoid, measuring 30 ft. across is thought to exist near the Sea of Fire, though none have ever seen it. A magmoid attacks by spraying a blast of superheated magma at opponents or by slamming into and rolling over them. It often targets weapon-wielding creatures first and moves close enough where they can hit with their weapons. The magmoid knows that more than likely should a weapon hit its fiery form, it will be turned into a pile of slag in short order.","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Mordnaissant","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Tiny","type":"undead","init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"lifesense"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":20,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+6 deflection, +2 Dex, +2 size","hp":94,"hd":"9d8+54","hdvalue":9,"fort":9,"ref":5,"will":10,"defensive_abilities":["channel resistance +2","shield of agony"],"immunities":["undead traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":5,"special":"cannot run"},{"type":"fly","speed":50,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 claws +10 (1d2-4)","ranged":"lash of fury +11","space":"2-1/2 ft.","reach":"0 ft. (30 ft. with lash)","special_attacks":[{"type":"death curse"},{"type":"lash of fury"},{"type":"pain wail"}],"strength":3,"dexterity":14,"intelligence":7,"wisdom":18,"charisma":23,"baseatk":6,"cmb":6,"cmd":18,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (lash of fury)"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (ray)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":19},{"skill":"Perception","value":18},{"skill":"Stealth","value":21}],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","twins","litter (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"Floating before you is a horrid, shriveled human fetus nested within a translucent sphere of dark energy. Its jet-black eyes glitter with intensity as it twitches and spasms slightly, as if in great pain.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Curse","kind":"Su","details":"As a final cruel jest to the individual that puts a mordnaissant out of its misery, the slayer must make a DC 20 Will save or suffer from a terrible curse that reduces all subsequent experience points awarded by 50%. The save DC is Charisma-based."},{"type":"Lash of Fury","kind":"Su","details":"The mordnaissant can lash out with its negative energy powers and directly attack the vitality of living creatures, in the form of a twisting stream of black energy. The mordnaissant must make a ranged touch attack against its target as an attack action. If the ray hits, the victim must make a DC 22 Fortitude save for half damage or duration, depending on the specific effect chosen by the mordnaissant. The save DC is Charisma-based. The lash of fury has a range of 30 ft. with no range increment. The mordnaissant can pick from three possible lashes; it must make its choice prior to rolling the attack. The three options are: whip the flesh (as inflict moderate wounds, 2d8+9 damage), whip the mind (1d4 points of Intelligence damage), or whip the soul (stun 1d4+1 rounds). A critical hit doubles the damage rolled or the duration, in the case of whip the soul."},{"type":"Lifesense","kind":"Su","details":"A mordnaissant notices and locates living creatures within 60 ft., just as if it possessed the blindsight ability."},{"type":"Pain Wail","kind":"Su","details":"As a swift action, the mordnaissant can produce a terrible wailing sound that reflects the pain it experiences every moment of its existence. All living creatures within 20 ft. must make a DC 20 Will save or be dazed for one round. For every 20 points of damage the mordnaissant takes, the save DC increases by +1."},{"type":"Shield of Agony","kind":"Su","details":"A mordnaissant harnesses the pain of its existence to shield it. It adds its Charisma modifier as a deflection bonus to its AC and CMD."}],"description":"Occasionally when a gravid woman dies violently in a place infused with unholy or negative energies, the unborn child within her doesn't perish, but instead continues to grow, vitalized by dark power, until it is capable of clawing its way free from its dead mother. This horrible creature, known as a mordnaissant, lives an existence of eternal pain, loneliness and suffering, relived only by its ability to inflict harm on those around it. Mordnaissants avoid bright light if they can, though they suffer no ill effects from it.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Originally appearing in Rappan Athuk Reloaded (© Necromancer Games, 2006)"},{"name":"Mustard Jelly","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"ooze","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"blindsight","modifier":"60 ft."}],"auras":["poison aura (10 ft., DC 21)"],"ac":17,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":17,"ac_mods":"+8 natural, -1 size","hp":105,"hd":"10d8+60","hdvalue":10,"fort":9,"ref":3,"will":3,"defensive_abilities":["divide","energy absorption"],"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["gaze attacks","paralysis","poison","polymorph","sleep","stunning","visual effects"],"resists":[{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":18,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"slam +9 (2d4+3 plus 1d4 acid)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"acid"},{"type":"constrict","details":"2d4+3 plus 1d4 acid"}],"strength":15,"dexterity":10,"constitution":22,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":10,"charisma":10,"baseatk":7,"cmb":10,"cmd":20,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":19},{"skill":"Stealth","value":9}],"environments":["temperate marshes"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears to be a yellowish-brown amoeba.","group":"Jelly","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Acid","kind":"Ex","details":"A mustard jelly secretes a digestive acid that dissolves only flesh. Any melee hit deals acid damage."},{"type":"Divide","kind":"Ex","details":"A mustard jelly can, as a standard action, split itself into two identical jellies, each with half of the original's current hit points (round down). A jelly with 10 hit points or less cannot divide itself. When divided, each jelly moves faster than the original (base speed 40 ft. per round)."},{"type":"Energy Absorption","kind":"Ex","details":"A mustard jelly is immune to electrical effects and magic missiles. If targeted by an electricity effect (including area effects) or a magic missile spell, the mustard jelly gains temporary hit points equal to the amount of damage it would have otherwise sustained. These temporary hit points last for 1 hour."},{"type":"Poison Aura","kind":"Ex","details":"The mustard jelly exudes an aura of poison in a 10-foot radius centered on it that slows (as the slow spell) any creature in the area as long as it remains in the area and for 1d4 rounds afterward if it fails a DC 21 Fortitude save. A new save must be made each round a creature is within 10 ft. of the mustard jelly. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Mustard jelly appears to be a yellowish-brown form of the ochre jelly and is thought to be a distant relative of said creature. However, the mustard jelly is far more dangerous than its supposed relative because it is intelligent.\n\nThe mustard jelly gives off a faint odor of mustard plants to a range of 20 ft. Though it possesses intelligence, a mustard jelly cannot speak.\n\nA mustard jelly attacks by forming a pseudopod from its body and either slashing or enveloping its foes. Mustard jellies prefer to attack from ambush or where they have the upper hand on an opponent. If combat goes against a mustard jelly, it doesn't hesitate to flee, though often it uses this tactic to lure unsuspecting foes in closer.\n\nA mustard jelly's natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Mustard Jelly originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Nabasu Demonling","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":23,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":22,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +12 natural","hp":73,"hd":"7d10+35","hdvalue":7,"fort":10,"ref":3,"will":8,"dr":"10/cold iron or good","immunities":["death effects","electricity paralysis","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":18,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"2 claws +11 (1d6+4), bite +11 (1d8+4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"death gaze","details":"DC 15"},{"type":"feed"},{"type":"sneak attack","details":"+2d6"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":7,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"deeper darkness","details":"10-ft. radius"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 lbs. of objects only"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"enervation"}]}],"strength":19,"dexterity":13,"constitution":20,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":16,"charisma":15,"baseatk":7,"cmb":11,"cmd":22,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":11},{"skill":"Fly","value":11},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":23},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":9},{"skill":"Stealth","value":10,"special":"+18 in shadowy areas"},{"skill":"Survival","value":13}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","plus one more","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"plane shift"}],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature is tall and thin with large, leathery, scaled, bat-like wings. Its skin is stretched tightly over its bones to the point that its underlying muscles can be seen clearly. Its skin is pale gray. Its hands end in long fingers tipped with razor-sharp talons. Its mouth is filled with tusk-like teeth, dominated by two overgrown tusks that jut upward from its bottom jaw. Its eyes glow with an eerie yellow light.","group":"Demon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Death Gaze","kind":"Su","details":"Once per day per growth point (minimum 1/day for a demonling, 10/day for a mature nabasu), a nabasu can use its death gaze for a full round. Living creatures within 20 ft. must succeed on a Fortitude save or gain a negative level. A humanoid slain in this manner transforms into a ghoul in 1d4 rounds under the control of the nabasu that created it. The save DC is Charisma-based. If the nabasu dies, any ghouls under its control become free-willed."},{"type":"Plane Shift","kind":"Su","details":"Three times per day a nabasu demonling can shift to the Material Plane, and a mature nabasu can shift between the Abyss and the Material Plane or back. This transports the nabasu and up to six other creatures provided they all link hands with the nabasu. It is otherwise similar to the spell of the same name (CL 10th for the demonling and CL 13th for the mature nabasu)."},{"type":"Feed","kind":"Su","details":"When a nabasu creates a ghoul with its gaze attack, it gains a growth point. It gains a bonus equal to its growth point total on attack rolls, CMB rolls, saving throws, caster level checks, and skill checks. Its maximum hit points increase by 10 for each growth point it gains and its caster level increases by 1. For every 2 growth points, its natural armor bonus, SR, and CR increases by +1. Each time it gains a growth point, the nabasu demonling makes a DC 30 caster level check-success indicates it becomes a mature nabasu. At 10 growth points, a demonling automatically becomes a mature nabasu."}],"description":"Nabasu (both plural and singular form) are one of the most malign of demonkind. They derive great pleasure from torturing and killing (albeit slowly) other creatures. Unlike other demons, a nabasu spends a portion of its life on the Material Plane. Those that reach the demonling stage in their growing process travel to the Material Plane where they feed on humanoids in order to continue their maturity. Once a nabasu reaches maturity, it returns to the Abyss to spend the rest of its immortal existence there. A nabasu (demonling or mature) stands 7 ft. tall and weighs about 700 pounds. Nabasu prefer to attack with their claws and bite so they can watch their opponents die a slow and very painful death. A nabasu fights until either it or its opponent is dead, and it never shows mercy to an opponent in battle.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Nabasu originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Netherspark","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["evil","extraplanar"],"init":7,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+3 Dex, +6 natural","hp":125,"hd":"10d10+70","hdvalue":10,"fort":12,"ref":10,"will":10,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["negative energy"],"resists":[{"type":"positive energy","value":16}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slam +14 (1d6+4)","ranged":"negative energy ray +13 touch (1 level, DC 22)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"negative energy aura"},{"type":"negative energy burst"},{"type":"negative energy ray"}],"strength":19,"dexterity":16,"constitution":24,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":16,"charisma":14,"baseatk":10,"cmb":14,"cmd":27,"feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (ray)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":16},{"skill":"Bluff","value":15},{"skill":"Climb","value":14},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":15},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":15},{"skill":"Linguistics","value":3},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Survival","value":15}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","and Infernal"],"environments":["any (Plane of Negative Energy)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature looks like a 6-foot tall humanoid whose form is composed of dark matter. Its head is featureless and sports no eyes, ears, nose, or mouth. It wears no clothes and bands of silver and white crackle and dance in its form.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Negative Energy Aura","kind":"Ex","details":"Being composed of negative energy, a netherspark radiates an aura of such energy in a 10-foot radius. Any living creature within this area takes 1 point of damage per round until it leaves the area. Undead in the area heal 1 hit point each round they remain in the area. Undead cannot more hit points than their normal total from the netherspark's aura."},{"type":"Negative Energy Burst","kind":"Su","details":"Once every 1d4 rounds, a netherspark can release a burst of negative energy in a 20-foot radius around it. Creatures in the area take 1d8+10 points of negative energy damage. Undead take no damage but heal a number of hit points equal to what the ray would otherwise deal."},{"type":"Negative Energy Ray","kind":"Su","details":"Once per round as a standard action, a netherspark can release a ray of negative energy with a rangte of 40 ft. as a ranged touch attack. A target hit takes gains one negative level if it fails a DC 22 Fortitude saving throw. On a successful save, the target avoids the negative level but still takes 1d8 points of negative energy damage. The save DC is Constitution-based."}],"description":"Nethersparks are natives of the negative energy plane that sometimes find themselves lost in the material plane where they seek to transform positive energy into a negative charge. On their home plane, they are attracted to living organisms, and seek to transform them into nothingness where both they and their home plane absorb the creature's positive essence. On the material planes these creatures are often found haunting graveyards or in the employ of a powerful necromancer. Undead creatures are attracted to, and can detect the presence of a netherspark within 60 ft.\n\nA netherspark stands about 6 ft. tall and weighs about 180 pounds. Its body is entirely composed of negative energy and dark matter. No facial features are discernable on its head, though the creature can see, hear, and speak.\n\nA netherspark begins combat using its negative energy ray before closing into melee range. In close combat, the creature rains blow after blow down on its adversaries with its powerful fists. The creature continually moves around during combat attempting to expose as many targets as possible to its negative energy aura. A netherspark's natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.\n\nA netherspark's natural weapons, as well as any weapon it wields, are treated as evil-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Niserie","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CN","size":"Medium","type":"fey","subtypes":["water"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":13,"ac_touch":13,"ac_flat_footed":10,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +1 dodge","hp":22,"hd":"4d6+8","hdvalue":4,"fort":5,"ref":6,"will":6,"defensive_abilities":["water form"],"sr":18,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"dagger +2 (1d4)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":7,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"control water"},{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"water breathing","details":"on another"}]}],"spellsprepared_caster_level":7,"spellsprepared_concentration":9,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"unholy blight"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bestow curse"},{"spell":"remove curse"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bear's endurance"},{"spell":"cure moderate wounds"},{"spell":"silence"},{"spell":"sound burst"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bane"},{"spell":"comprehend languages"},{"spell":"cure light wounds"},{"spell":"doom"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"bleed"},{"spell":"create water"},{"spell":"purify food and drink"},{"spell":"resistance"}]}],"strength":10,"dexterity":14,"constitution":14,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":15,"charisma":18,"baseatk":2,"cmb":2,"cmd":15,"feats":[{"feat":"Dodge","type":"bonus"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":11},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":11},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":8},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":8},{"skill":"Perception","value":9},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":9},{"skill":"Sleight of Hand","value":7},{"skill":"Stealth","value":7,"special":"+15 in water"},{"skill":"Swim","value":8}],"languages":["Aquan","Sylvan"],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"}],"environments":["any aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","gang (3-6)"],"treasure":"standard (dagger)","description_visual":"Reclining on a rock in the surf is a gorgeous and voluptuous female humanoid with long golden hair, pearly white skin, and blue eyes. She is clad in soft, silk-like cloth of white and gold.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Spells","details":"Niserie can cast divine spells as 7th-level clerics. They don't gain access to domains or other cleric abilities."},{"type":"Water Form","kind":"Ex","details":"As a standard action, a niserie can turn into a mobile pool of water. This functions like gaseous form, except that the niserie cannot fly in this form. It retains its own base speed, and its swim speed doubles to 80 ft. The niserie can remain in her water form for a number of minutes equal to twice her Constitution bonus and can end this ability as a standard action. A spell with the cold descriptor inflicts no damage on a niserie in its water form, but instead automatically slows the creature as per the spell for 1d6 rounds or until she leaves her water form. A spell with the electricity, fire, or sonic descriptor inflicts normal damage on a niserie in its water form."}],"description":"Niserie (also called undine or true undine) are playful and mischievous fey. On occasion they are malicious, taking great pleasure in luring sailors to their watery graves. Also known as sea nymphs, niserie prefer trickery to combat and flee if presented with overwhelming odds.\n\nNiserie stand from 5 to 6 ft. tall and weigh around 130 pounds. They are always female; there are no male niserie (that scholars are aware of). While most niserie have golden hair, the rare niserie has seaweed green hair with moss green eyes.\n\nIf forced into combat, a niserie defends herself with her spell-like abilities and dagger, seeking escape at the earliest convenience by changing into water and flowing away.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Northlands Aurochs","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"animal","init":0,"senses":[{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":8,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+12 natural, -2 size","hp":105,"hd":"10d8+50 (+10)","hdvalue":10,"fort":14,"ref":7,"will":4,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40}],"melee":"gore +16 (2d8+15)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"powerful charge","details":"gore +18, 4d8+15"},{"type":"stampede"},{"type":"trample","details":"2d8+15, DC 25"}],"strength":30,"dexterity":10,"constitution":21,"intelligence":2,"wisdom":13,"charisma":7,"baseatk":7,"cmb":19,"cmd":29,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Endurance"},{"feat":"Great Fortitude"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (gore)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":20}],"environments":["any (Northlands forests)","any plains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","herd (3-12)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This massive ox is as tall as a man at the shoulders. Its coat is black with a pale stripe down its spine. Great lyre-shaped horns sweep forward from its bony brow.","group":"Aurochs","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Stampede","kind":"Ex","details":"A frightened herd of aurochs (3 or more) flees as a group in a random direction (but always away from the perceived source of danger). They literally run over (as an overrun that doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity) anything of size Gargantuan or smaller that is in their path, but no CMB check is necessary, and the target cannot choose to let them pass without taking any damage. The stampede deals 5d6 points of damage for every two aurochs in the herd (rounded up). Any victims of the stampede can make a DC 25 Reflex save for half damage. The save DC is Strength-based."}],"description":"These massive aurochs (singular and plural) are prehistoric cattle that once roamed the plains and forests of the world in vast herds but are now on the verge of extinction, being found only in the primeval forests and remote places of the Northlands where their horns are prized trophies of the hunt-though many a hunter has fallen beneath their spearlike horns and crushing hooves in the attempt. Massive beasts, these prehistoric aurochs have been used as symbols of fertility and strength for many cults down through the ages appearing in decoration from the crudest cave paintings to ornate temples. When captured they command a high price for use in the arenas of cosmopolitan regions, though they often take a heavy toll among the matadors who face them.\n\nNorthlands aurochs stand 6 ft. or more high at the withers with their heads rising 2 ft. above that. Their characteristic lyre-shaped horns extend upward another 2 ft. They grow up to 18 ft. long and can weigh as much as 8,000 pounds. Males have a black coat with a pale stripe down the spine, and females and calves have a reddish coat. A light load for a Northlands aurochs is up to 3,200 pounds; a medium load 3,201-6,400 pounds; and a heavy load 6,401-9,600 pounds. An aurochs can drag 48,000 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"Original author Greg A. Vaughan/Kenneth Spencer  Originally appearing in Northlands Saga 3: The Death Curse of Sven Oakenfist (© Frog God Games/Kenneth Spencer, 2011)"},{"name":"Oil Shark","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","subtypes":["aquatic","extraplanar","fire"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"Blindsense","modifier":"30 ft."},{"type":"keen scent","modifier":"180 ft."}],"ac":19,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +9 natural, -2 size","hp":85,"hd":"10d10+30","hdvalue":10,"fort":10,"ref":9,"will":6,"dr":"5/ -","immunities":["fire"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to cold"],"speed":[{"type":"swim","speed":60}],"melee":"bite +14 (2d6+9)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","strength":23,"dexterity":15,"constitution":17,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":12,"charisma":2,"baseatk":10,"cmb":18,"cmd":31,"feats":[{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Vital Strike"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":13,"special":"+21 vs. grapple"},{"skill":"Perception","value":8},{"skill":"Swim","value":20}],"environments":["any (Plane of Fire; Sea of Fire)","any (Plane of Molten Skies; Sea of Fire)"],"organizations":["solitary","school (2-5)","pack (6-11)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"An immense, eyeless shark over 20 ft. long ft. darts through the flames, its blackish-blue, metallic scales gleam with blackish oil.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Keen Scent","kind":"Ex","details":"An oil shark can notice creatures by scent in a 180-foot radius and detect blood in oil or water at ranges of u p to one mile."}],"description":"The Sea of Fire located on the Plane of Molten Skies and the Plane of Fire is home to strange aquatic life (if they can be called that), but perhaps none is stranger than the mighty oil shark. These creatures spend their days swimming beneath the burning surface of the Sea of Fire, searching for prey. Their diet consists of other aquatic creatures found in the Sea of Fire such as fire crabs, oil worms, and the great fire whales. The latter is a particular favorite of the oil shark, and while the typical great fire whale outweighs (and is generally larger) than the typical oil shark, an oil shark pack has been known to attack and kill with ease a lone fire whale. Oil sharks have never been encountered outside the Plane of Molten Skies or Plane of Fire though sages believe the oil shark can exist in normal water. Oil sharks are completely blind and rely completely upon their \"sonar\" to hunt their prey. Oil sharks generally behave as other sharks; circling their prey before striking with their powerful jaws. Non-aquatic prey (i.e., creatures that breathe air) are often grasped in its jaws and dragged below the surface of the burning sea where it drowns in the oily waters. Their oily hides allow them to glide smoothly and quickly through normal water. Oil sharks are a delicacy of volcano giants and are often hunted by such creatures. The thick, metallic hide of an oil shark is prized by salamanders and they often hunt these creatures, kill them, and sculpt armor from the hide. Oil Shark Armor (Medium Armor) Because of the natural oily nature of the metal in an oil shark's scales (which retain these properties even after its death), a creature suffers no penalty to Swim checks for wearing this armor and also adds a +5 bonus to all Escape Artist checks. In addition, a creature wearing oil shark armor is unaffected by obstructions such as webs (magical or otherwise). Oil Shark Armor: Cost 1,000 gp (usually can't be bought); Armor Bonus +6; Maximum Dex Bonus +2; Armor Check Penalty -4; Arcane Spell Failure 30%; Speed 20 ft. (Base 30 ft.), 15 ft. (Base 20 ft.); Weight 40 lb.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Pestilential Cadaver","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"construct","init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"auras":["disease (30 ft., DC 15)"],"ac":19,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +8 natural","hp":64,"hd":"8d10+20","hdvalue":8,"hp_mods":["fast healing 5"],"fort":2,"ref":3,"will":2,"dr":"5/magic","immunities":["construct traits (+20 hp)","magic"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"2 slams +12 (1d8+3 plus sickness)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"disease aura"},{"type":"sickness"}],"strength":16,"dexterity":12,"intelligence":10,"wisdom":10,"charisma":12,"baseatk":8,"cmb":11,"cmd":22,"feats":[{"feat":"Ability Focus (disease)"},{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Stealthy"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (slam)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Disguise","value":7},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":3},{"skill":"Perception","value":6},{"skill":"Stealth","value":13}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","Infernal (cannot speak any languages)"],"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature appears to be an animated corpse composed of mismatched body parts, crudely stitched together. Maggots and worms writhe from its rotting form.","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Disease Aura","kind":"Ex","details":"A pestilential cadaver exudes a putrid aura in a 30-foot radius around itself. Creatures entering or caught in the area must succeed on a DC 15 Fortitude save or contract one of the diseases listed on the table below. A creature that saves is immune to the disease aura of that pestilential cadaver for one day. The save DC is Charisma-based. 1D8 DISEASE 1 Blinding sickness 2 Cackle fever 3 Filth fever 4 Mindfire 5 Red ache 6 Shakes 7 Slimy doom 8 Roll twice, ignoring any results of 8."},{"type":"Fast Healing","kind":"Ex","details":"A pestilential cadaver's fast healing only works if it is within 30 ft. of a fresh corpse. A fresh corpse is defined as any living creature killed within the last 24 hours."},{"type":"Immunity to Magic","kind":"Ex","details":"A pestilential cadaver is immune to any spell or spell-like ability that allows spell resistance. In addition, certain spells and effects function differently against the creature, as noted: A magical attack that deals fire damage dazes a pestilential cadaver (as the daze spell) for 3 rounds (no save). A magical attack that inflicts disease heals the cadaver of 1d6 hit points per level of the spellcaster. A remove disease spell deals 1d6 points of damage per caster level (maximum 10d6) to a pestilential cadaver. The creature can attempt a Fortitude save to reduce the damage by half. A heal spell functions as a harm spell against a pestilential cadaver."},{"type":"Sickness","kind":"Ex","details":"A living creature hit by a pestilential cadaver's slam attack must succeed on a DC 15 Fortitude save or become sickened for 2d6 rounds. A creature that fails its save by 5 or more is must immediately attempt another DC 15 Fortitude save or be subjected to one of the diseases above just as if it had been affected by the cadaver's aura. A creature that succeeds on the second Fortitude save isn't subject to the disease effects of this ability for one day, even if it fails any subsequent Fortitude saves by 5 or more. The save DC is Charisma-based."}],"description":"The pestilential cadaver is literally a walking disease, a construct formed from the bodies of those who died of plague and fever. It is ever active, seeking to spread its contagion to all who live. It rots constantly, losing flesh to decomposition, but gaining material from those it slays.\n\nAlthough it moves awkwardly, in fits and jerks, the pestilential cadaver is as swift and dexterous as a healthy man, even capable of running (though it rarely does so). It stands about 6 ft. in height, and weighs roughly 150 pounds.\n\nThe pestilential cadaver engages in combat primarily as a means of infecting new victims and absorbing their diseased remains once it slays them. It is a straightforward combatant, deadly even to those it doesn't touch.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Protector","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"LN","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar","lawful"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"know alignment","modifier":"50 ft."}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +6 natural","hp":55,"hd":"7d10+14","hdvalue":7,"fort":9,"ref":9,"will":11,"immunities":["outsider traits"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":50}],"melee":"longsword +9 (1d8+2 /19-20)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":7,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":9,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"8/day","spells":[{"spell":"resistant touch"},{"spell":"touch of law"}]}],"spellsprepared_caster_level":7,"spellsprepared_concentration":9,"spellsprepared":[{"spell_level":4,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"chaos hammer"},{"spell":"divine power"},{"spell":"spell immunity","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":3,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"daylight"},{"spell":"magic circle against chaos"},{"spell":"protection from energy","type":"domain"},{"spell":"remove curse"}]},{"spell_level":2,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"aid"},{"spell":"align weapon"},{"spell":"consecrate"},{"spell":"resist energy"},{"spell":"shatter"},{"spell":"shield other","type":"domain"}]},{"spell_level":1,"spell_slots":1,"spells":[{"spell":"bless"},{"spell":"bless water"},{"spell":"command"},{"spell":"divine favor"},{"spell":"endure elements"},{"spell":"protection from chaos","type":"domain"},{"spell":"sanctuary"}]},{"spell_level":0,"spell_slots":99,"spells":[{"spell":"create water"},{"spell":"cure minor wounds"},{"spell":"detect magic"},{"spell":"read magic"}]}],"spelldomains":"Law, Protection","strength":15,"dexterity":15,"constitution":15,"intelligence":20,"wisdom":20,"charisma":20,"baseatk":7,"cmb":9,"cmd":21,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Expertise"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":15},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":9},{"skill":"Heal","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (any one)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (the planes)","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (religion)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":15},{"skill":"Spellcraft","value":12},{"skill":"Survival","value":15}],"languages":["Auran","Celestial","Common","telepathy 50 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"air walk"}],"environments":["any (Inner Planes)","any (Outer Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","troupe (6-11)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature resembles a tall, powerful human with green eyes and a bald head. It is dressed in long, flowing green robes that seem to billow as though blown by an invisible and unfelt gentle breeze.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Air Walk","kind":"Su","details":"Protectors can air walk as the spell of the same name (caster level 10th). This ability is always active and can be dispelled, but the protector can restart it as a free action on its next turn."},{"type":"Know Alignment","kind":"Su","details":"A protector automatically knows the alignment of any creature within 50 ft. that it looks upon."},{"type":"Resistant Touch","kind":"Sp","details":"As a standard action, you can touch an ally to grant him your resistance bonus for 1 minute. When you use this ability, you lose your resistance bonus granted by the Protection domain for 1 minute."},{"type":"Touch of Law","kind":"Sp","details":"You can touch a willing creature as a standard action, infusing it with the power of divine order and allowing it to treat all attack rolls, skill checks, ability checks, and saving throws for 1 round as if the natural d20 roll resulted in an 11."}],"description":"Protectors are extraplanar guardians of law that appear as very noble and regal creatures. They are often sent to the Material Plane when the forces of chaos swing from the balance. Protectors move by means of their air walk ability; their feet never touch the ground, and they always float 6 to 10 inches above the ground. A protector stands 7 ft. tall and weighs about 200 pounds or more.\n\nProtectors attack neutral (except non-intelligent or low-intelligence creatures such as animals) and chaotic creatures on sight. They never knowingly and willingly attack lawful creatures. A protector fights with its longsword and spells.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Protector originally appeared in the First Edition module B3 Palace of the Silver Princess (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission.","gear":"longsword"},{"name":"Shadow Demon","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["chaotic","demon","evil","extraplanar","incorporeal"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":18,"ac_flat_footed":14,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +4 deflection, +0 natural","hp":59,"hd":"7d10+21","hdvalue":7,"fort":5,"ref":11,"will":7,"defensive_abilities":["incorporeal"],"dr":"10/cold iron or good","immunities":["cold","electricity","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"fire","value":10}],"sr":18,"weaknesses":["sunlight powerlessness"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":40,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 claws +11 touch (1d6 plus 1d6 cold), bite +11 touch  (1d8 plus 1d6 cold)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"pounce"},{"type":"sprint"},{"type":"shadow blend"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":10,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":13,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"deeper darkness"},{"spell":"fear"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self only"},{"spell":"telekinesis"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"magic jar"},{"spell":"summon","details":"level 3, 1 shadow demon 50%"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"shadow conjuration"},{"spell":"shadow evocation"}]}],"dexterity":18,"constitution":17,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":14,"charisma":19,"baseatk":7,"cmb":11,"cmd":29,"feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Combat Reflexes"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Acrobatics","value":14},{"skill":"Bluff","value":14},{"skill":"Fly","value":22},{"skill":"Knowledge (local)","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":12},{"skill":"Perception","value":20},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":14}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","any two","telepathy 100 ft."],"environments":["any (Abyss)"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","haunt (3-8)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"Only this shadowy bat-winged demon's teeth and claws have any sense of physicality to them-the rest is lost in darkness.","group":"Demon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Sprint","kind":"Ex","details":"Once per minute, a shadow demon increase its fly speed to 240 ft. for 1 round."},{"type":"Shadow Blend","kind":"Su","details":"During any conditions other than bright light, a shadow demon can disappear into the shadows as a move-equivalent action, effectively becoming invisible. Artificial illumination or light spells of 2nd level or lower don't negate this ability."},{"type":"Sunlight Powerlessness","kind":"Ex","details":"A shadow demon is utterly powerless in bright light or natural sunlight and flees from it. A shadow demon caught in such light cannot attack and can take only a single move or attack action. A shadow demon that is possessing a creature using magic jar isn't harmed by sunlight, but if it is struck by a sunbeam or sunray spell while possessing a creature, the shadow demon is driven out of its host automatically."}],"description":"Shadow demons resemble standard shadows with wings. They are the incorporeal form of a demon trapped in the form of a shadow as punishment for some wrongdoing. If anything can release a demon trapped in shadow form, only the dukes, princes, and lords of the Abyss know such secrets. As a result of their new form, shadow demons are malign and evil, destroying all life they encounter.\n\nA shadow demon lurks in dark places, waiting for its prey to pass nearby. Often before leaping to attack, it uses its deeper darkness to gain the advantage. It then leaps from the shadows and attacks with its incorporeal attacks. It selects the most powerful foe in a group and uses its magic jar against it.\n\nA shadow demon's natural weapons, as well as any weapons it wields, are treated as chaotic-aligned and evil-aligned for the purpose of overcoming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Shadow Demon originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Shedu","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"LG","size":"Large","type":"magical beast","init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +6 natural, -1 size","hp":76,"hd":"9d10+27","hdvalue":9,"fort":9,"ref":7,"will":11,"sr":16,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"2 hooves +13 (1d6+5)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","spell_like_abilities_caster_level":9,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"astral projection","details":"self only"},{"spell":"detect evil"},{"spell":"detect thoughts"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"charm monster"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":12,"constitution":17,"intelligence":16,"wisdom":16,"charisma":17,"baseatk":9,"cmb":19,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. bull rush","cmd":36,"cmd_special":"+2 vs. bull rush, +4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Blind-Fight"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":15},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":15},{"skill":"Fly","value":9},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":14}],"languages":["Celestial","Common","Draconic","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"ethereal jaunt"}],"environments":["any warm land"],"organizations":["herd (2-8)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This creature has the body of a chestnut-colored horse, large brownfeathered wings, and the head and face of a bearded human. Its long beard and hair is straight-braided.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Ethereal Jaunt","kind":"Su","details":"A shedu can shift from the Ethereal Plane to the Material Plane as a free action, and shift back again as a move-equivalent action. This ability is otherwise identical with the ethereal jaunt spell (caster level 18th)."}],"description":"Shedus are good creatures found roaming the Material Plane seeking out evil and destroying it wherever and whenever they encounter it.\n\nShedus aid good creatures in need and never knowingly associate with evil creatures. They are on good terms with lammasu and ki-rin. Shedu found on the Material Plane make their homes in abandoned and ruined temples and shrines dedicated to gods of law and good.\n\nShedu rarely enter combat, but always come to the aid of good creatures in need. Shedu relentlessly attack evil on sight, using a combination of their hooves and spell-like abilities.\n\nPriests and holy men sometimes seek the advice and wisdom of a shedu and will journey great distances to find the knowledge they seek. Some ancient cults even worship and pray to the shedu holding them up as deities in their culture.\n\nA typical shedu is about 8 ft. long and weighs about 500 pounds.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Shedu originally appeared in the pre-First Edition book Eldritch Wizardry (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1976) and later in the First Edition Monster Manual (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1977) and is used by permission.  The Greater Shedu originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Soul Eater","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["extraplanar"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"find target"}],"ac":25,"ac_touch":17,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+6 Dex, +1 dodge, +8 natural","hp":75,"hd":"10d10+20","hdvalue":10,"fort":9,"ref":13,"will":3,"dr":"10/magic","immunities":["critical hits","paralysis","poison","sleep","stun"],"speed":[{"type":"fly","speed":100,"maneuverability":"perfect"}],"melee":"2 claws +16 (1d6+1/19-20 plus 1d6 Wis damage)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"soul drain"},{"type":"Wisdom damage"}],"strength":13,"dexterity":22,"constitution":14,"intelligence":12,"wisdom":11,"charisma":11,"baseatk":10,"cmb":11,"cmd":28,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Dodge"},{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Critical (claw)"},{"feat":"Weapon Finesse"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":13},{"skill":"Fly","value":18},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":14},{"skill":"Perception","value":17},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":16},{"skill":"Stealth","value":19,"special":"+29 in darkness, smoke, or concealment"},{"skill":"Survival","value":13}],"languages":["telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"link to caster"}],"environments":["any land","any underground","any (Lower Planes)"],"organizations":["solitary"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This creature resembles a billowing cloud of inky darkness. Two long, pale white arms protrude from the cloud, each ending in a clawed hand.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Find Target","kind":"Sp","details":"When ordered to find a creature, a soul eater does so unerringly, as though guided by discern location. The being giving the order must have seen the creature to be found and must know the target's name. This ability is the equivalent of an 8th-level spell."},{"type":"Link to Caster","kind":"Ex","details":"When a soul eater is summoned to the Material Plane, it creates a mental link between itself and the caster who summoned it. If a soul eater's victim (i.e., the creature it is summoned to slay) is killed before the creature can devour its soul, the soul eater returns at full speed to the caster and attacks him. Likewise, if a soul eater is defeated in battle (but not slain) by its target, the creature returns to the caster and attacks him. So long as both the caster and soul eater are on the same plane of existence, the soul eater can successfully locate the caster (again as though guided by discern location). If the caster leaves the plane, the link is temporarily broken. Once the caster returns, or the soul eater enters a plane the caster is on, the link is immediately restored."},{"type":"Soul Drain","kind":"Su","details":"When a soul eater slays a foe, it devours the victim's soul. Such a creature cannot be returned to life by any means save a deity's intervention."},{"type":"Wisdom Damage","kind":"Su","details":"A creature hit by a soul eater's claw attack must succeed on a DC 17 Fortitude save or take 1d6 points of Wisdom damage. The save DC is Constitution-based. A creature brought to Wisdom 0 dies."}],"description":"A soul eater is an extraplanar creature of great power. Its plane of origin is unknown but is thought to be some sort of void plane. Soul eaters are summoned to the Material Plane for one purpose-to slay living creatures. When given a target, a soul eater can track it unerringly. Soul eaters sustain themselves on the life energies of living creatures and derive this sustenance by draining the souls of living targets. A soul eater strikes with two ghostly claws in each round. It attacks until either it or its target is defeated or slain. A soul eater's natural weapons are treated as magic weapons for the purpose of over coming damage reduction.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Soul Eater originally appeared in the First Edition module X4 Master of the Desert Nomads (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Storm Drake","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":5,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"},{"type":"storm vision"}],"ac":20,"ac_touch":10,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":84,"hd":"8d12+32","hdvalue":8,"fort":10,"ref":7,"will":9,"immunities":["paralysis","sleep"],"resists":[{"type":"electricity","value":20}],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30},{"type":"fly","speed":60,"maneuverability":"average"}],"melee":"bite +13 (2d6+6/19-20), 2 claws +13 (1d6+6)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"lightning breath"},{"type":"savage bite"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":12,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"control weather"},{"spell":"control winds"}]},{"frequency":"3/day","spells":[{"spell":"call lightning"},{"spell":"fog cloud"},{"spell":"obscuring mist"},{"spell":"sleet storm"}]}],"strength":22,"dexterity":13,"constitution":18,"intelligence":8,"wisdom":12,"charisma":13,"baseatk":8,"cmb":15,"cmd":26,"feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Fly","value":10},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":12},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":6},{"skill":"Perception","value":12},{"skill":"Stealth","value":8},{"skill":"Survival","value":8}],"languages":["Draconic"],"sq":[{"type":"speed surge"}],"environments":["temperate mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","pair","wing (3-8)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This powerful dragon is dull gray in color and sports massive wings. Its mouth is lined with razor-sharp fangs the length of daggers.","group":"Drake","source":"Tome of Horrors 4 (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Lightning Breath","kind":"Su","details":"A storm drake can, as a standard action, breathe a ball of electricity that explodes upon contact with a solid surface or target. This attack has a range of 100 ft. and deals 7d6 points of electricity damage (DC 18 Reflex half) to all creatures within a 20-foot radius spread. Once a storm drake has used its lightning breath, it cannot do so again for 1d6 rounds. The save DC is Constitution-based."},{"type":"Savage Bite","kind":"Ex","details":"A storm drake applies 1-1/2 times its Strength bonus to damage dealt with its bite attack, and it threatens a critical hit on a 19-20."},{"type":"Speed Surge","kind":"Ex","details":"Three times per day as a swift action, a storm drake may draw on its draconic heritage for a boost of strength and speed to take an additional move action in that round."},{"type":"Storm Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A storm drake can see through fog, clouds, and similar obscuring effects with perfect clarity, including areas affected by spells such as obscuring mist and fog cloud."}],"description":"Storm drakes are fierce creatures that make their lairs high atop storm-ravaged mountains. From here, they can survey their territory, and dive to the attack when a potential meal is spotted. Favored meals include humanoids of all kinds, and large game such as deer, elk, and moose.\n\nStorm drakes are generally 20 ft. long from nose to tail and weigh over 3,000 pounds. Colors range from dark, dull gray to slate gray mottled with lighter grays. Claws and talons are black and its eyes are the color of dark storm clouds. Storm drakes typically live 300 years.\n\nA storm drake is merciless in combat, biting and slashing its foes with its dagger-like teeth and claws. An ambush hunter by nature, a storm drake's approach is usually foreshadowed by a sudden shift in the weather from clear or slightly overcast skies to dark skies and storms.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Tallow Golem","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Medium","type":"construct","init":-1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"}],"ac":18,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"-1 Dex, +9 natural","hp":75,"hd":"10d10+20","hdvalue":10,"fort":3,"ref":2,"will":21,"dr":"10/adamantine and bludgeoning","immunities":["cold","construct traits"],"weaknesses":["vulnerability to fire"],"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20}],"melee":"2 slams +13 (2d8+3 plus grab)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"chemisorb"}],"strength":16,"dexterity":9,"wisdom":11,"charisma":1,"baseatk":10,"cmb":13,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grapple","cmd":17,"environments":["any"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-4)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This human-sized automaton has been carved from wax. Its face bears no discernible features and appears as a completely smooth surface.","group":"Golem","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Chemisorb","kind":"Ex","details":"A tallow golem can break down and absorb chemicals from a living victim by making a successful grapple check. If it pins the foe, it deals 1d4 points of Constitution damage each round the pin is maintained. Additionally, this causes skin discoloration. The victim must make a successful DC 17 Fortitude save or take 1 point of Charisma drain. Whether the save succeeds or fails, that victim cannot be affected again by the skin discoloration of that tallow golem's chemisorb attack for 24 hours. The save DC is Constitution-based and includes a +2 racial bonus."}],"description":"The tallow golem is a humanoid construct composed entirely of wax. It stands about 6 ft. tall and usually bears no facial features, unless the creator chooses to render a lifelike \"wax dummy,\" in which case the golem can appear quite real indeed. Wizards who specialize in the creation of tallow golems refer to themselves as \"chandlers.\" Unlike other golemsculptors, chandlers consider their work a form of art. The golem wears whatever clothing (if any) that its creator desires, usually rags or trousers. It has no possessions and no weapons. The golem cannot speak or utter any sound. It moves slowly, but relentlessly. A tallow golem attacks by pounding its foes with its massive fists. Construction The tallow golem is formed from a large block of candle wax mixed with special powders worth at least 500 gp. TALLOW GOLEM CL 14th; Price 13,000 gp Requirements Craft Construct, geas/quest, limited wish, resist energy (cold), creator must be caster level 14th; Skill Craft (sculptures) DC 19; Cost 6,750 gp","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Tendrul","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"NE","size":"Large","type":"aberration","subtypes":["aquatic"],"init":2,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"keen scent"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":12,"ac_flat_footed":18,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +1 dodge, +9 natural, -1 size","hp":76,"hd":"9d8+36","hdvalue":9,"fort":6,"ref":5,"will":8,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":10},{"type":"swim","speed":40}],"melee":"bite +10 (1d8+5 plus grab), tail slap +5 (1d6+2)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"constrict","details":"1d8+5"},{"type":"gnashing of teeth"}],"strength":21,"dexterity":15,"constitution":17,"intelligence":3,"wisdom":12,"charisma":6,"baseatk":6,"cmb":13,"cmd":26,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Improved Iron Will"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":11},{"skill":"Swim","value":16}],"sq":[{"type":"amphibious"}],"environments":["temperate aquatic","warm aquatic"],"organizations":["solitary","school (3-8)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"The size of a small whale, this amphibious creature has a pair of powerful flippers with which it pulls itself from the waters to sun itself on the stones. It has a head reminiscent of a piranha, the body of a giant grayish-black seal, and a bony razor-sharp scythe-like tail.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Gnashing of Teeth","kind":"Ex","details":"If a tendrul scores a natural 20 on its attack roll with its bite attack and subsequently confirms the critical hit, it deals triple normal damage."},{"type":"Keen Scent","kind":"Ex","details":"A tendrul notices creatures by scent in a 90-foot radius and detects blood in the water at ranges of up to 500 ft."}],"description":"The tendrul is a horror of the semi- and subtropical shallows, often attacking fishermen who wade out into the shallows with their nets, or wander out to search their crab traps. A tendrul makes its home in the shallows of the water, sleeping in underwater caves or between rocks.\n\nDuring the daylight hours on warmer days, it isn't uncommon to see a tendrul sunning itself on the rocks or sands. Though it can survive indefinitely on land, a tendrul prefers the sanctity of its watery home, leaving the waters only to sun on the rocks or feed on some unlucky fisherman or creature that has wandered too close to the shoreline.\n\nA tendrul looks like a hideous cross between a seal and piranha. An average tendrul reaches 12 ft. long and weighs several hundred pounds.\n\nIts body is grayish-black with it being lighter on its underbelly and a bit darker on the head. Its trunk tapers off into a thin, scythe-like tail of hardened bone, dark gray in color. Its piranha-like head sports a gaping maw filled with razor-sharp dagger-sized teeth of grayish-yellow. A tendrul sustains itself on fish, aquatic life, and oceanic plants in the water, but prefers a diet of flesh from land-bound creatures. It especially savors the flesh of humans and goblins.\n\nA tendrul's favorite tactic is to bury itself in the silt and sand of the shoreline and wait for a fisherman to wander over its hiding place where it rises up from beneath its prey, biting it, and devouring it on the spot.\n\nAmphibious, it isn't uncommon for a tendrul to chase wounded prey some distance onto the shore to finish it off.\n\nAnother favored tactic a tendrul employs is to grab prey in its mouth, drag it into the water and pin it underwater where the tendrul holds it until its prey drowns.","ecology":"","habitat_society":""},{"name":"Tormentor Devil","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"LE","size":"Medium","type":"outsider","subtypes":["devil","evil","extraplanar","lawful"],"init":8,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"detect thoughts"},{"type":"see in darkness"}],"ac":24,"ac_touch":14,"ac_flat_footed":20,"ac_mods":"+4 Dex, +10 natural","hp":76,"hd":"8d10+32","hdvalue":8,"hp_mods":["regeneration 5 (good, silver)"],"fort":6,"ref":10,"will":5,"dr":"5/good or silver","immunities":["fire","poison"],"resists":[{"type":"acid","value":10},{"type":"cold","value":10}],"sr":18,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"+1 ghost touch battleaxe +13 (1d8+5/x3) or 2 claws +12 (1d8+4)","ranged":"soulcatcher net +12 (1d6 plus grapple)","space":"5 ft.","reach":"5 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"ghost touch"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":12,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":16,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"constant","spells":[{"spell":"detect thoughts"}]},{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"dimensional anchor"},{"spell":"doom"},{"spell":"greater teleport","details":"self plus 50 pounds of objects only"},{"spell":"scorching ray"}]},{"frequency":"1/day","spells":[{"spell":"order's wrath"}]}],"strength":18,"dexterity":18,"constitution":18,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":14,"charisma":15,"baseatk":8,"cmb":8,"cmd":24,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Alertness"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Bluff)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":16},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":13},{"skill":"Escape Artist","value":15},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (planes)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":15},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":15},{"skill":"Survival","value":13,"special":"+17 tracking"}],"languages":["Abyssal","Common","Infernal","telepathy 100 ft."],"sq":[{"type":"soul track"}],"environments":["any (Hell)"],"organizations":["pack (2-5)","troupe (pack plus 1-4 hell hounds)"],"treasure":"none","description_visual":"This reddish-gray scaled humanoid stands taller than a human. Its hands are clawed and its feet cloven. Oversized fangs jut from its upper jaw and drip foul-smelling saliva. Small horns protrude from just above its eyes, curving backwards. Its head and body are hairless and a small curving tail trails behind it. It wields a battleaxe and carries a wickedly-barbed net slung across its back.","group":"Devil","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Ghost Touch","kind":"Ex","details":"A tormentor devil deals damage normally with its claws against incorporeal creatures."},{"type":"Soul Track","kind":"Su","details":"A tormentor devil can track the soul of any creature that enters any of the planes of Hell. Tracking a soul has a base DC of 20 and follows the rules for tracking. A tormentor devil must be on the same plane as the soul it is tracking. Soulcatcher Net: A tormentor devil's net looks like a normal net and follows the rules for net attacks. The net has 20 hit points; the Escape Artist check to get free is DC 30; the net can be broken with a successful DC 30 Strength check. The net can entrap incorporeal creatures. The net has many small razor-sharp barbs lining it. These barbs deal 1d6 points of damage each round to any creature caught in the net, including incorporeal creatures. (The incorporeal creature's 50% chance to avoid damage from a corporeal source doesn't apply to this attack.)"}],"description":"Tormentors of Souls, known as tormentor devils, make their way across the uppermost plane of Hell searching for souls that have entered the realms of evil. Various arch-devils and dukes employ tormentor devils to capture and return souls to them for their devilish uses. Tormentors often employ hell hounds when pursuing renegade or runaway souls.\n\nTormentors stand 7 ft. tall and weigh about 400 pounds.\n\nTormentor devils attack using their battleaxes and nets. They hunt in packs when tracking souls and are rarely encountered alone. If leading a pack of hell hounds, tormentors let the hell hounds attack first while they stay at range and attack with their nets.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","gear":"+1 ghost touch battleaxe, soulcatcher net"},{"name":"Tunnel Worm","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Huge","type":"magical beast","init":1,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"60 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"tremorsense","modifier":"60 ft."}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":15,"ac_mods":"+1 Dex, +7 natural, -2 size","hp":112,"hd":"9d10+54 (+9)","hdvalue":9,"fort":12,"ref":9,"will":5,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":20},{"type":"burrow","speed":20}],"melee":"bite +14 (2d6+9 plus grab)","space":"15 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rend armor"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":13,"constitution":22,"intelligence":1,"wisdom":10,"charisma":6,"baseatk":9,"cmb":17,"cmb_special":"+4 vs. grappling","cmd":28,"cmd_special":"can't be tripped","feats":[{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Lightning Reflexes"},{"feat":"Toughness"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Weapon Focus (bite)"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":15}],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","cluster (2-5)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"This massive creature appears to be a 30-foot long sleek black centipede with a long segmented body and many slender legs. Its huge mandibles are serrated and razor-sharp, and its eyes are multi-faceted. A ring of chitinous bone protects its oversized head.","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Rend Armor","kind":"Ex","details":"If a tunnel worm grapples an opponent wearing armor, it attempts to chew away the armor with its powerful mandibles. With a successful grapple check it deals double its regular bite damage to the opponent's armor. Creatures not wearing armor are unaffected by this special attack. Armor reduced to 0 hit points is destroyed."}],"description":"The tunnel worm is a burrowing creature related to the monstrous centipede. It is a very aggressive predator and hunter, though it can sustain itself by scavenging. Its preferred food is fresh, raw meat. Tunnel worms are very aggressive and attack anything that enters their territory.\n\nTunnel worms live in mazelike complexes of burrows connected by passages they have chewed out over time; these burrows are often filled with the rotting remains of past prey, used by the worm to incubate its offspring. The favored tactic of the tunnel worm is to lurk beneath the surface of the ground or behind a wall until it senses a creature moving by, whereupon it burrows out to surprise and attack its prey (treat this attack as a charge attack). A tunnel worm that has taken more than half its hit points in damage retreats to its lair unless it is cornered, in which case it fights to the death.\n\nA typical tunnel worm is 30 ft. long, but can grow to a length of 60 ft.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Tunnel Worm originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."},{"name":"Two-headed Troll","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"CE","size":"Large","type":"humanoid","subtypes":["giant"],"init":0,"senses":[{"type":"darkvision","modifier":"90 ft."},{"type":"low-light vision"},{"type":"scent"}],"ac":16,"ac_touch":9,"ac_flat_footed":16,"ac_mods":"+7 natural, -1 size","hp":95,"hd":"10d8+40 (+10)","hdvalue":10,"hp_mods":["fast healing 1"],"fort":11,"ref":3,"will":5,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":30}],"melee":"longsword +12 (2d6+6), longsword +12 (2d6+6), 2 bites +7 (1d8+3) or 2 claws +12 (1d6+6), 2 bites +12 (1d8+6)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"10 ft.","special_attacks":[{"type":"rend","details":"2 claws, 1d6+9"},{"type":"superior two-weapon fighting"}],"strength":22,"dexterity":11,"constitution":19,"intelligence":9,"wisdom":10,"charisma":6,"baseatk":7,"cmb":14,"cmd":24,"feats":[{"feat":"Cleave"},{"feat":"Iron Will"},{"feat":"Power Attack"},{"feat":"Skill Focus (Perception)"},{"feat":"Toughness"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Perception","value":18}],"languages":["Giant"],"environments":["any underground"],"organizations":["solitary","gang (2-4)","warband (1-2 twoheaded trolls plus 2-4 trolls)"],"treasure":"standard","description_visual":"The most discernible feature of this massive brute is its two heads. Its hide is mottled green-gray and covered in coarse, dark hair. Each head is identical: red eyes, drooping nose, and yellow fangs. Its arms and legs end in razor-sharpened claws.","group":"Troll","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Superior Two-Weapon Fighting","kind":"Ex","details":"A two-headed troll fights with a weapon in each hand. Because each of its two heads controls an arm, the two-headed troll doesn't take a penalty on attack or damage rolls for attacking with two weapons."}],"description":"The two-headed troll is thought to be the hideous offspring of an ettin and female troll. Sages contend that no other explanation is possible concerning this monster. Two-headed trolls prefer to make their lairs underground and away from civilization. Although believed to be the offspring of an ettin and troll, they don't associate with the former, but are often found leading the latter during raids or wars. A two-headed troll stands about 10 ft. tall and weighs about 2,000 pounds. Its hide is mottled green or gray, and its facial features resemble that of a standard troll. Two-headed trolls typically dress in rags or tattered clothes or even battered and rusted armor on occasion. Their legs end in three-toed ft., and their powerful arms end in sharpened claws. The two-headed troll has the slow moving gait of the normal troll, but doesn't walk hunched over. Two-headed trolls attack with two claws and two bites, though on occasion they have been known to wield longswords or clubs.","as_character":[{"description":"Two-headed troll characters possess the following racial traits.","racial_traits":[{"type":"Ability Score Bonuses","value":"+12 Strength, +8 Constitution, -2 Intelligence (minimum 3), -4 Charisma."},{"type":"Large size","value":"-1 penalty to Armor Class, -1 penalty on attack rolls, -4 penalty on Stealth checks, +1 bonus on CMB and CMD checks, lifting and carrying limits double those of Medium characters."},{"type":"Space/Reach","value":"10 ft./10 ft."},{"type":"Darkvision","value":"Two-headed trolls can see in the dark out to 90 ft."},{"type":"Low-light vision","value":"Two-headed trolls can see twice as far as humans in conditions of dim light."},{"type":"Scent","value":"Two-headed trolls can detect opponents within 30 ft. by sense of smell."},{"type":"Racial Hit Dice","value":"A two-headed troll begins with ten levels of humanoid, which provide 10d8 Hit Dice, a base attack bonus of +7, and base saving throw bonuses of Fort +7, Ref +3, and Will +3."},{"type":"Racial Skills","value":"A two-headed troll's humanoid levels give it skill points equal to 10 x (2 + Int modifier, minimum 1). A two-headed troll's two heads give it a +2 racial bonus on Perception checks."},{"type":"Racial Feats","value":"A two-headed troll's humanoid levels give it five feats."},{"type":"AC","value":"+7 natural armor bonus."},{"type":"Natural Weapons","value":"Two-headed trolls fight with 2 claws (1d6) and 2 bites (1d8)."},{"type":"Special Attacks","value":"Rend, superior two-weapon fighting."},{"type":"Special Qualities","value":"fast healing 1."},{"type":"Languages","value":"Two-headed trolls begin play speaking Giant. Two-headed trolls with high Intelligence scores can choose from the following languages: Common, Orc."}]}],"ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Two-Headed Troll originally appeared in the First Edition Fiend Folio (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1981) and is used by permission.","gear":"2 longswords"},{"name":"Young Cloud Dragon","cr":7,"xp":3200,"alignment":"N","size":"Large","type":"dragon","subtypes":["air"],"init":6,"senses":[{"type":"cloud vision"},{"type":"dragon senses"}],"ac":21,"ac_touch":11,"ac_flat_footed":19,"ac_mods":"+2 Dex, +10 natural, -1 size","hp":76,"hd":"8d12+24","hdvalue":8,"fort":9,"ref":8,"will":10,"speed":[{"type":"land","speed":40},{"type":"fly","speed":200,"maneuverability":"poor"}],"melee":"bite +12 (2d6+7), 2 claws +12 (1d8+5), 2 wings +7 (1d6+2), tail slap +7 (1d8+7)","space":"10 ft.","reach":"5 ft. (10 ft. with bite)","special_attacks":[{"type":"breath weapon","details":"40 ft. cone, DC 17, 6d6 cold plus bull rush [Tiny or smaller]"}],"spell_like_abilities_caster_level":8,"spell_like_abilities_concentration":11,"spell_like_abilities":[{"frequency":"at-will","spells":[{"spell":"create water"}]}],"strength":21,"dexterity":14,"constitution":17,"intelligence":14,"wisdom":15,"charisma":14,"baseatk":8,"cmb":15,"cmd":25,"cmd_special":"+4 vs. trip","feats":[{"feat":"Flyby Attack"},{"feat":"Hover"},{"feat":"Improved Initiative"},{"feat":"Wingover"}],"skills":[{"skill":"Bluff","value":13},{"skill":"Diplomacy","value":13},{"skill":"Fly","value":7},{"skill":"Intimidate","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (arcana)","value":13},{"skill":"Knowledge (nature)","value":13},{"skill":"Perception","value":13},{"skill":"Sense Motive","value":13}],"languages":["Auran","Aquan","Common","Draconic"],"environments":["temperate mountains","warm mountains"],"organizations":["solitary","clan (2-5)"],"treasure":"triple standard","description_visual":"This dragon has a fringed and frilled head and wings that sweep back from its shoulders to its tail. Large, piercing rose colored eyes dominate its somewhat triangular head. Its tail trails off becoming misty and translucent near the tip.","group":"Dragon","source":"Tome of Horrors Complete (3pp)","special_abilities":[{"type":"Breath Weapon","kind":"Su","details":"A cloud dragon's breath weapon is a powerful cone of icy cold air. When a cloud dragon uses its breath weapon, make a single bull rush attack using the dragon's CMB against the CMD of any creature that failed its Reflex save and is three or more size categories smaller than the dragon. This bull rush doesn't provoke attacks of opportunity, and the dragon cannot choose to move with any opponent pushed back. In addition to being pushed back, affected creatures are knocked prone and take 1d4 points of nonlethal damage per 10 ft. they are pushed back. Flying creatures are buffeted and pushed back twice the distance and sustain 1d6 points of nonlethal damage per 10 ft. they are pushed back."},{"type":"Cold Bite","kind":"Su","details":"At old age, a cloud dragon's bite deals an additional 2d6 points of cold damage. An ancient dragon's damage increases to 4d6, and a great wrym's to 6d6."},{"type":"Cloud Form","kind":"Su","details":"As a standard action, a juvenile or older cloud dragon can assume gaseous form at will, but it can remain gaseous indefinitely and has a fly speed of 20 ft. with perfect maneuverability."},{"type":"Cloud Vision","kind":"Ex","details":"A very young cloud dragon can see perfectly in foggy conditions (such as those created by fog cloud or obscuring mist)."},{"type":"Immunity to Winds","kind":"Su","details":"A cloud dragon is immune to the effects of wind. It ignores the penalties applied to the Fly skill incurred by wind speed, and is immune to the negative effects of any spell or effect that manipulates wind, such as gust of wind and whirlwind. Spell-like Abilities A cloud dragon gains the following spelllike abilities, usable at will upon reaching the listed age category. Young-create water; Juvenile-obscuring mist; Adult-stinking cloud; Old-call lightning; Ancient-control winds; Great Wyrm-control weather."},{"type":"Whirlwind","kind":"Sp","details":"A great wyrm cloud dragon can use this ability three times per day. It works as a whirlwind spell. This ability is the equivalent of an 8th-level spell."}],"description":"Cloud dragons are the most reclusive of all dragons, rarely leaving the safety and sanctity of their cloudy lairs. They have a great dislike for non-flying creatures and creatures that must use non-natural means to fly (such as through magical items or spells). A cloud dragon wyrmling's scales are silvery-blue with a slight hint of red at the tip of each scale. As the dragon ages, its color slowly changes to a bright sunset orange. The oldest cloud dragons resemble gold dragons, save for the large bony plates on their heads and backs. Cloud dragons are not highly aggressive, but dislike interlopers and attack them on sight. They open combat using their breath weapon, followed by their spell-like abilities. A cloud dragon rarely lands, preferring to fight from the air.","ecology":"","habitat_society":"","credit":"The Cloud Dragon originally appeared in the First Edition Monster Manual II (© TSR/Wizards of the Coast, 1983) and is used by permission."}];
